From bccc70bfce97378fa35327858b527d4e14a30b0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y.z>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:14:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/21] dtb: select the GENI debug UART for
 qcom,geni-debug-uart consoles

init_early now attaches SerialKind::QcomGeni when the stdout-path node is
compatible with qcom,geni-debug-uart and its MMIO range covers the SE
registers. The divider is only reprogrammed when the node carries an
explicit clock-frequency; the mainline binding's GCC clock has no fixed
rate. A node whose SE firmware is not UART is not attached, and
skip-init attaches without touching registers.

Adds an SDM845 uart9-shaped DT fixture (alias stdout-path, QUP wrapper
with identity ranges) and tests that run the discovery path against the
GENI register model.

Co-Authored-By: Cursor <noreply@cursor.com>
